<div style="background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center; border: 2px solid #1a5276;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Talents Around Us</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> I Will Play the Drums in the Parade.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: reading_1: Create written reflections on stories read in class. reading_2: Analyze characters' actions and motives in stories. phonemic_awareness: Demonstrate knowledge of phonemic awareness by distinguishing spoken rhyming words from non-rhyming words.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can write reflections on stories about Panamanian traditions and Fiestas Patrias (e.g., 'The girl felt proud wearing the traditional pollera dress in the parade.' 'The boy enjoyed playing the drums for the school band.'). Can analyze characters' actions and motives in stories about Fiestas Patrias celebrations (e.g., 'Liz practiced the traditional dance to perform in the parade.' 'Liz was chosen as the abanderada to lead the parade because she earned the top honor roll for being the best student in the class.'). Can distinguish rhyming words from non-rhyming words in simple comparisons (e.g., 'drum' and 'hum' vs. 'march' and 'flag').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="background-color: #e0f2f7; border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows pictures of Panamanian Fiestas Patrias parades, different musical instruments (drums, accordion, flute), and students marching with a flag. The teacher asks, "What do you see in the pictures?" "What instruments can these students play?" "Who wants to perform in a parade?" and "What will you do?" to activate prior knowledge and introduce the theme of talents and parades.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher holds up a picture of a student playing the drums and says, "This student *can play the drums*. He *will play* the drums in the *parade*. He is very *talented*." The teacher models the pronunciation of key vocabulary like 'parade', 'drums', 'talented', 'celebrate', and future simple ('will play'). The teacher also introduces simple rhyming words related to the theme, like 'drum' and 'hum', and non-rhyming words, like 'march' and 'flag', for phonemic awareness.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding with questions such as:
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can the boy in the picture play the guitar?" (Expected answer: "No, he can play the drums.")</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is he sad about the parade?" (Expected answer: "No, he is excited.")</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do 'drum' and 'hum' rhyme?" (Expected answer: "Yes.")</li>
            </ul></p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(5-7 min)</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "The Talents Around Us"</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short narrative story excerpt titled "Maria's Parade Dream" about a student participating in Fiestas Patrias celebrations.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Story Excerpt:</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">"Meet Maria. She is a dedicated *honor roll student*. Maria *can play the flute* beautifully. She *will play* the flute in the *Panamanian National Holidays parade* this year. Her school *band* is very *talented*. If Maria *practices* every day, she *will perform* amazingly. She feels very *excited* to represent her school. Her goal is to make her family proud and *celebrate* our country's *Patriotic Celebrations*. She *needs to* rehearse with her *performer* friends and *try* her best. The *audience* *will* be huge!"</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will understand the main idea and specific details of a short narrative text about Fiestas Patrias, identifying characters' abilities, plans, and motives.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> The teacher reads the story aloud, then asks students to read silently.
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the story about?" "Who is Maria?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read statements and decide if they are true or false based on the story (e.g., "Maria can play the drums." [False], "Maria will play in the parade." [True]).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Match characters' names (Maria) with their talents (plays the flute) and future plans (will perform in the parade).</li>
            </ul></p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(10-12 min)</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Reading</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice identifying and understanding key vocabulary (e.g., 'honor roll student', 'flute', 'parade', 'band', 'talented', 'excited', 'practice', 'perform', 'celebrate') and grammatical structures (Future simple tense with 'will', First conditional with 'if...will', modal 'can' for ability) within the context of the story. They will also practice distinguishing rhyming words.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
            <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice – "Story Gap-Fill":</b> Students receive a worksheet with sentences from "Maria's Parade Dream" containing blanks. They choose words from a provided box (e.g., 'flute', 'parade', 'practices', 'excited', 'can play', 'will perform') to complete the sentences, ensuring they understand context and vocabulary.
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><em>Example: Maria ______ the flute beautifully. (can play) If she ______ every day, she ______ amazingly. (practices, will perform)</em></p></li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice – "Grammar Spotter":</b> Students reread the story individually. They are instructed to:
                    <ul style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Underline all sentences that show Maria's *future plans* (using 'will').</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Circle all verbs that show Maria's *ability* (using 'can').</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Draw a box around any *first conditional* sentences ('If... will...').</li>
                    </ul></li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Check & Rhyme Challenge:</b> In pairs, students compare their answers from the "Grammar Spotter" activity, reading specific sentences to each other and justifying their choices. Additionally, the teacher provides a list of words from the story (e.g., 'drum', 'band', 'flag', 'march'). Pairs take turns identifying rhyming words ('drum' / 'hum') and non-rhyming words ('flag' / 'march'), stating "These words rhyme" or "These words do not rhyme."</li>
            </ul></p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(15-18 min)</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "The Talents Around Us"</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> "My Parade Star Reflection" – Students will write a short reflection and analysis about Maria from the story "Maria's Parade Dream."</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students are given a graphic organizer or a few guiding questions to help them structure their written reflection, ensuring they focus on the reading objectives.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Guiding Questions:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What talent does Maria have? (e.g., "Maria *can play the flute*.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What will Maria do in the Panamanian National Holidays parade? (e.g., "She *will perform* with her *band*.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Why do you think Maria practices every day? What is her motive? (e.g., "Her motive is to make her family proud and *celebrate*.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How does Maria feel about the parade? (e.g., "She feels very *excited*.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What happens if Maria practices every day? (e.g., "If she practices, she *will perform* beautifully.")</li>
                    </ul></li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students write their reflections, aiming to use target vocabulary and grammar structures encountered in the story. They focus on analyzing Maria's actions and motives, and expressing their understanding of her plans.</li>
            </ul></p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(8-10 min)</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> The teacher will use an observation checklist and a simple rubric to evaluate the students' written reflections and their ability to distinguish rhyming words during an oral check.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their "My Parade Star Reflection" for evaluation. The teacher will also conduct a quick oral check of rhyming word distinction with a few students.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Reading_1 (Reflection):</b> Clearly writes reflections on the story, using details about Maria.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Reading_2 (Analysis):</b> Accurately analyzes Maria's actions (e.g., practicing, performing) and motives (e.g., making family proud, celebrating).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> Uses target vocabulary (e.g., 'honor roll student', 'flute', 'parade', 'excited', 'talented', 'celebrate') appropriately.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Attempts to use future simple ('will'), first conditional ('if...will'), and modal 'can' to express ability.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Phonemic Awareness:</b> Can distinguish rhyming words from non-rhyming words when prompted (e.g., 'drum' and 'hum' vs. 'flag' and 'march').</li>
            </ul></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete the following sentences on a small slip of paper:
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing Maria wants to do in the parade is _____. Her main motive is _____."</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can now identify _____ words in a story."</li>
            </ul></p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(5 min)</p>
        </td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What did you learn about analyzing a character's actions and motives from Maria's story?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of the story did you find most interesting or easy to understand?"</li>
            </ul></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What aspects of the reading lesson worked well? Did students effectively create written reflections and analyze character actions/motives?</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Were the grammar structures (future simple, first conditional, 'can') and target vocabulary successfully identified and understood within the reading context?</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds might be needed for students who struggled with comprehension or analysis? (e.g., providing sentence starters for reflections, more visual aids for understanding motives).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How well did students distinguish rhyming words?</li>
            </ul></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson focused on reading about others' talents and parade plans. The next lesson (Lesson 3: Speaking & Interaction) will provide opportunities for students to actively speak and interact, sharing their own talents, expressing plans using future simple, and discussing possibilities with the first conditional.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(2-3 min)</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>